## CORRECTION (2026-08-02) — supersedes parts of Issue 1 below

1. **The 14 July auth commits are NOT in prod.** Prod runs v1.11.0 (`865a600`) = v1.10.2 + landing copy only; `cd70131` (signing-key rotation) and `a960eba` (Postgres OTP store) live only on `fix/tenant-2-readiness` (verified: `git merge-base --is-ancestor` fails; live bundle probed). The mass-logout "Leg A = key rotation" claim is withdrawn — the logout cause is ordinary 14-day cookie expiry. Deploy note for later: when that branch DOES ship, it will invalidate all existing OTP/passkey sessions once (expected, communicate it).
2. **New fault found (Issue 1b): magic-link callback loop.** The affected member RECEIVES the email — quota starvation is not their blocker. Clicking the link bounces them back to email entry. Ranked causes, with evidence: (1) HIGH — link opened in a different browser/in-app mail viewer than the one that requested it: `localStorage "emailForSignIn"` is absent, the callback falls back to a bare `window.prompt` (auth-callback.tsx:26) which many webviews suppress → error → back to sign-in → new link → loop; (2) stale/re-clicked one-time links compounding the loop; (3) browser discarding the session cookie (silent middleware 307 loop, live-verified with a bogus cookie); (4) email case mismatch — send route lowercases, localStorage stores raw case (sign-in-form.tsx:95); (5) `verifySessionCookie` rejection. Scanner prefetch is unlikely to consume links (GET doesn't consume the oobCode). Conclusive discrimination: member's two answers (same browser? which mail service?) or Cloud Run request logs for their timestamps (`GET /auth/callback` → `POST /api/auth/session` → dashboard status pattern).
3. **Member unblock today (no deploy):** long-press the button in the email → Copy link → paste into the SAME browser they typed their email into; use only the newest sign-in email; if prompted, enter the email all-lowercase; avoid private windows. Note: do NOT steer them to the PWA OTP path — prod's OTP store is still an in-memory per-instance Map on scale-to-zero Cloud Run, so OTP verify can legitimately fail (fixed by the unshipped `a960eba`).
4. **Minimal fixes for the loop (add to the Issue 1 `fix:` release):** replace `window.prompt` with a proper email-confirmation form on `/auth/callback`; map Firebase error codes to specific messages with one-click resend; verify the cookie actually landed before redirecting (else show cookie guidance); lowercase email at both capture points; preserve the redirect param in the dashboard bounce; add Sentry capture to the callback catch (currently console-only — why this was invisible).

